<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
Personal data such as social security numbers, dates of birth and salaries, as well as
passwords, should not be stored in a database in cleartext. Anyone who can read the database,
a backup of it, or the result of an injection attack against it can then read the data directly.
</p>
<p>
This query reports SQL <code>INSERT</code>, <code>UPDATE</code>, <code>REPLACE</code>,
<code>UPSERT</code> and <code>MERGE</code> statements executed through <code>database/sql</code>
(or another modeled SQL library) whose query text or bind parameters contain data whose name
suggests it is sensitive, unless the data was first passed through a hashing or encryption function.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Hash passwords with a password-specific adaptive hash function such as Argon2id, bcrypt or scrypt.
Encrypt other sensitive data that must be recoverable, for example with an authenticated cipher
such as AES-GCM and a key that is not stored alongside the data. Avoid storing sensitive data at
all if the application does not need it.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>
In the following example, the social security number of a user is written to the database in
cleartext (BAD), and in the second function it is encrypted before it is stored (GOOD).
</p>
<sample language="go">
func storeUser(db *sql.DB, user User) {
	// BAD: the SSN is stored in cleartext
	db.Exec("INSERT INTO users (name, ssn) VALUES (?, ?)", user.Name, user.SSN)
}

func storeUserSafely(db *sql.DB, user User) {
	// GOOD: the SSN is encrypted before it is stored
	db.Exec("INSERT INTO users (name, ssn) VALUES (?, ?)", user.Name, encrypt(user.SSN))
}
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>OWASP: <a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html">Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet</a>.</li>
<li>OWASP: <a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html">Password Storage Cheat Sheet</a>.</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
